 "notes": "Headline result: light-shining-through-wall exclusion on hidden-photon kinetic mixing chi (black 'UWA 2013' region of Fig. 5), extracted from the vector polygon in the e-print figure chiV2_cropped.pdf with axes calibrated on tick labels. Deepest point recovers chi=1.68e-7 at m=5.28e-5 eV, matching the quoted chi<1.7e-7 at 53 ueV (12.76 GHz TM020 mode). Limit rises as ~m^-2 toward low mass (curve clipped at chi~1e-4 at plot top, m~5.2e-6 eV) and terminates at the resonance mass, where the final point closes the excluded wedge along the vertical edge. Laboratory LSW bound: no dark-matter density assumed. The paper's separate single-mass CDM hidden-photon limits (chi<6.14e-14 homogeneous / 5.32e-15 inhomogeneous at 53 ueV) are not the reported curve. Confidence level not stated in the paper; 0.95 assumed.",
